---
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { resolveSiteHref } from '../lib/paths';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Learn how this generic Forge starter is structured and how to make it your own.">
  <Container size="md" class="pb-16">
    <article class="prose mx-auto">
      <div class="badge badge-outline">About this starter</div>
      <h1>A useful foundation, not a finished identity.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Forge provides an approachable structure for a content-driven website while leaving its subject, voice, and visual identity up to you.</p>

      <h2>What to replace first</h2>
      <p>Start with the typed site configuration, then replace these example articles with material that reflects your project. Shared layouts and metadata will update every route consistently.</p>

      <h2>What is already connected</h2>
      <p>Semantic navigation, responsive layout primitives, local fonts, theme-aware styling, canonical metadata, a sitemap, an RSS feed, and automated accessibility checks are ready to extend.</p>

      <p>
        <a href={resolveSiteHref('/articles/')}>Explore the example articles</a> or return to the
        <a href={resolveSiteHref('/')}>homepage</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </Container>
</BaseLayout>
